        <p class="profile-detail-region">Battle · Ancient Near East</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Kadesh</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">Year 5, third month of Shemu, day 9 of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramesses-ii">Ramesses II</a>, generally dated to May 1274 BCE by the low chronology; the high chronology puts it about 20 years earlier</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orontes-river">Orontes River</a> upstream of Lake <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homs">Homs</a>, near the stronghold of Kadesh, on what is now the Lebanon-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> border</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Egyptian Empire under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramesses-ii">Ramesses II</a>, in four divisions (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amun">Amun</a>, Re, Set and Ptah) with Sherden troops and the Ne'arin; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muwatalli-ii">Muwatalli II</a> with allies, among them Rimisharrinaa, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">Chariots</a> on both sides together are put at 5,000 to 6,000</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egyptians">Egyptians</a> drove the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittites</a> back across the Orontes, but the Hittites kept Kadesh. Modern historians describe a stalemate, and each side claimed the victory.</span></div>
        </div>
